<% @title = "Making requests" %>

<%# The ids missing_body and eir are linked to from core. %>
<%= page_band %>
<%= render :partial => 'sidebar' %>
<div id="left_column_flip" class="left_column_flip">
  <dl>

    <dt id="which_authority">Which authority should I ask? <a href="#which_authority" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Start from the <a href="<%= topics_path %>">topics</a>: each one says
        which kind of authority holds what, and where it's already published.
        Each authority's page also lists what it usually holds.</p>
      <p>If you ask the wrong one, it should tell you who to ask instead.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="missing_body">An authority is missing <a href="#missing_body" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Use the <a href="<%= new_change_request_path %>">form for adding an
        authority</a>. Give its name and, if you can find it, the email
        address it uses for Freedom of Information requests.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="authorities">Which organisations can I ask? <a href="#authorities" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Public authorities covered by the Freedom of Information Act, the
        Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act or the Environmental Information
        Regulations, and some organisations that answer requests voluntarily.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="focused">How do I write a good request? <a href="#focused" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Ask for recorded information, not opinions. Be specific: name the
        period, the place and the kind of record. A short, focused request is
        answered faster and is less likely to be refused on cost.</p>
      <p>Before you send, the site shows documents already published by that
        authority that match what you've written, and common questions from
        the topics.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="fees">Do I have to pay? <a href="#fees" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Requests are free. An authority can refuse a request that would cost
        too much to answer, or ask for a fee in a few cases, and it must tell
        you if it does.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="quickly_response">How quickly will they reply? <a href="#quickly_response" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Normally within <%= AlaveteliConfiguration.reply_late_after_days %>
        working days. The request page shows the due date, and moves it if the
        authority asks you to clarify or extends the time as the law allows.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="no_response">They haven't replied in time <a href="#no_response" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>The request page offers to send a reminder. If that doesn't work,
        you can ask for an internal review, and then complain to the
        regulator.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="not_satifised">I'm not happy with the reply <a href="#not_satifised" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Ask the authority for an internal review. If you're still unhappy,
        you can complain to the regulator.
        <a href="<%= help_unhappy_path %>">More about what to do</a>.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="reuse">Can I reuse what they send me? <a href="#reuse" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Information released under Freedom of Information law is yours to
        read, but copyright stays with whoever owns it. Check the authority's
        terms before republishing.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="ico_help">Who can help if something goes wrong? <a href="#ico_help" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>The regulator for the law your request was made under: the
        Information Commissioner for the Freedom of Information Act and the
        Environmental Information Regulations, and the Scottish Information
        Commissioner for Scottish authorities.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="data_protection">Can I ask for information about myself? <a href="#data_protection" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Not here. Information about yourself is a subject access request
        under data protection law: ask the authority directly, not on this
        site.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="private_requests">Are my requests private? <a href="#private_requests" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Yes. Only you and the site's administrators can read them. Documents
        are published only after checking. See the
        <a href="<%= help_privacy_path %>">privacy page</a>.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="eir">What are the Environmental Information Regulations? <a href="#eir" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>A separate law for information about the environment, such as air
        quality, pollution, land use or waste. It covers some organisations
        the Freedom of Information Act doesn't, and lets authorities extend
        the time to reply for complex requests.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="multiple">Can I send the same request to several authorities? <a href="#multiple" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Yes, as a batch request, if an administrator has allowed it for your
        account. Each authority gets its own copy, and replies are filed
        separately.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="offsite">They replied by post or phone <a href="#offsite" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Scan a paper reply and add it to the request, or note what was said,
        so the record is complete.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="moderation">Who checks what is published? <a href="#moderation" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>The site's administrators check every document and its details
        before it's published, including any redactions.</p>
    </dd>

  </dl>

  <div id="hash_link_padding"></div>
</div>
